From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Apr 2026 10:35:00 +0800
Subject: media: qcom: camss: Recognize VID_IF_BRIDGE entities in pipeline walk

camss_find_sensor_pad() only stops at MEDIA_ENT_F_CAM_SENSOR when
walking the pipeline to find the source entity. Devices that register
as MEDIA_ENT_F_VID_IF_BRIDGE (e.g. the Toshiba TC358743 HDMI-to-CSI-2
bridge) are therefore never found, which causes camss_get_link_freq()
and camss_get_pixel_clock() to fail with -ENODEV.

Treat VID_IF_BRIDGE entities the same way as CAM_SENSOR so that
bridge-based video capture pipelines work correctly.

Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -4614,7 +4614,8 @@ struct media_pad *camss_find_sensor_pad(struct media_entity *entity)
 
 		entity = pad->entity;
 
-		if (entity->function == MEDIA_ENT_F_CAM_SENSOR)
+		if (entity->function == MEDIA_ENT_F_CAM_SENSOR ||
+		    entity->function == MEDIA_ENT_F_VID_IF_BRIDGE)
 			return pad;
 	}
 }
